  "question_stem": "A car travels along a straight road with constant acceleration. It passes through points $A$, $B$ and $C$. The car passes point $A$ with velocity $14 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$. The two sections $AB$ and $BC$ are of equal length. The times taken to travel along $AB$ and $BC$ are $5 \\text{ s}$ and $3 \\text{ s}$ respectively.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$AB = 70 + 12.5a$, $AC = 112 + 32a$; using $AC = 2AB$ gives $a = 4\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$"
  ],
